  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Minor in News Studies"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Minors",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Minors",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/minors/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "The Minor in News Studies is designed to give students an understanding of journalism theory and practice. It comprises courses that introduce students to the basic skills of journalism; that delineate the history, practice, theory and ethical standards of the profession that allow them to combine both theory and practice in exploring specific areas of content and media."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Administered by: School of Journalism"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Exclusions: This minor is not available to students in the following programs:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Journalism",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Journalism",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/programs/fcad/journalism/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "To receive this Minor, students must complete six (6) courses from the following curriculum:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "One (1) Required course:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "NNS 101 Introduction to News Studies ( or JRN 103 )",
